# Authorization Rules

- Authorization MUST be enforced server-side for every protected resource and command.
- Roles currently include Commerce, Driver, and Administrator; finer permissions may be layered without weakening isolation.
- A commerce user MUST only access data owned by or explicitly shared with its business scope.
- A driver MUST only access delivery information permitted for operational execution.
- Administrators may operate across tenants only through explicit privileged permissions.
- Never rely on hidden UI buttons for access control.
- Authorization MUST be checked again during offline synchronization of commands/events.
